    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d746-a2">

                <pb facs="0709" n="611" xml:id="pg611"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Salisbury to Mr.
                            White.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-04-10"><hi rendition="#italic">April 10,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 17th ultimo respecting Mr. R. M. Geldart’s shipments on
                    board the <hi rendition="#italic">Beatrice, Mashona</hi>, and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Maria</hi>, and to inform you that it has been sent to
                    the high commissioner for South Africa.</p>
                <p>I do not think that the British authorities will be able to meet Mr. Geldart’s
                    suggestion that the cotton-seed oil should be purchased by them for the amount
                    of the invoice price, together with a fair profit on the transaction, as it
                    appears to me unlikely that they would be able to make any use of a vegetable
                    oil of this nature.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Salisbury.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
